From 162c56f1bbee753f50e4ef6f7cd04505b0e689f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nerduser13-ux <288021437+nerduser13-ux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:25:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recognize Word auto-numbered reference lists; add --inspect;
 safe splitting of runs with page-break render hints

Fixes the real-world case (RALF document) where the References heading was
found but 0 entries were parsed because the reference list is Word
auto-numbered (w:numPr via the 'List Number' style; numbers not in text).

- document_reader: load_numbering_map() (word/numbering.xml: numId ->
  abstractNum -> lvl start/numFmt), paragraph_numpr_info() (direct pPr or
  style chain incl. basedOn), compute_list_numbers() (visible number per
  paragraph, decimal lists only, document-wide sequence as Word renders).
- reference_parser: entries may be typed numbers OR Word list numbers (typed
  wins when both present); block detection counts auto-numbered paragraphs.
- word_footnotes: runs containing w:lastRenderedPageBreak (zero-width
  render hint) are now safe to split; the replacement preserves original w:t
  segmentation and places render hints at their original text positions.
- main: --inspect read-only diagnostic (per-line: idx/number/typed-or-list/
  URLs/text + resulting number->URL map + likely-cause hints).
- tests: +5 (auto-numbered list, bullet list NOT entries, typed-beats-list,
  page-break hint single + multiple citations) - 44/44 pass.
- Verified on the user's RALF document: 5 references, 7/7 footnotes
  inserted, 0 unresolved, 0 ambiguous, validation PASS, input hash
  unchanged.
- README: documents auto-numbered list support + --inspect.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
